# MCQ Practice Service Data Integration Phase 2

The goal is to implement persistent exam-taking logic for MCQ practice sessions, matching the experience of public exams with server-synced answers, audio feedback, and confetti effects.

## Proposed Changes

### Core Logic

#### [NEW] [use-practice-exam-attempt.ts](file:///c:/Users/User/Documents/monorepo-new/apps/home/modules/services/hooks/use-practice-exam-attempt.ts)
- Create a custom hook to manage practice session state.
- Handle answer submissions via `trpc.home.demoExam.submitAnswer`.
- Handle session completion via `trpc.home.demoExam.submitPractice`.
- Track performance metrics (correct, wrong, streak, score).

### Frontend Components

#### [MODIFY] [mcq-practice-service.tsx](file:///c:/Users/User/Documents/monorepo-new/apps/home/modules/services/ui/views/mcq-practice-service.tsx)
- Add `createPracticeSession` mutation.
- When "Start Practice" is clicked, call the mutation and redirect to the practice view with the `attemptId`.
- Toggle between configuration view and practice view if `attemptId` is present in URL.

#### [MODIFY] [take-mcq-practice-view.tsx](file:///c:/Users/User/Documents/monorepo-new/apps/home/modules/services/ui/views/take-mcq-practice-view.tsx)
- Update to use `use-practice-exam-attempt` hook.
- Implement server-synced answering.
- Add audio feedback (correct/wrong) and confetti effects for streaks.

## Verification Plan

### Automated Tests
- N/A

### Manual Verification
1. Navigate to MCQ practice config.
2. Select subjects and start practice.
3. Verify a persistent session is created in the DB.
4. Answer questions and verify they are saved to the server (refresh and check).
5. Complete the session and verify results.

